      "notes": [
        {
          "stage": "SILHOUETTE",
          "why": "layout GRID from the EDGE_TO_EDGE recipe rot6-mid (HOLDS); primitive NGON from the FACET member — a filled polygon — mass with a countable number of sides. LINE..CUBIC are always stroked whatever stroke says.",
          "composition": "rot6-mid measured ink 0.9154 with the PLATE probe, estimated 0.681 for a FACET mark (x0.74), against a DENSE target of 0.55",
          "member": "read from the direction: \"angular\"",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].layout",
            "fields[n].primitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "FOCAL_HIERARCHY",
          "why": "4 registers and sizeMax 40, both from the measured recipe rather than from a density word. Registers 1..3 carry the composition and register 0 carries the market.",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].sizeMax",
            "fieldCount, and the site budget"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "NEGATIVE_SPACE",
          "why": "spreadMax 128 from the recipe. Spread is a CEILING the seed draws beneath from a bytecode floor of 16, which is why the recipe pins it on the later registers: unpinned, one seed in twelve draws low and is a centred island in a collection that bleeds.",
          "consulted": "fields[n].spreadMax"
        },
        {
          "stage": "RHYTHM",
          "why": "symmetry ROT6 from the recipe — it is a project constant and carries no per-token variety, which is why the recipe rather than a seed decides it; count PINNED at 12 because the drive is not COUNT",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].symmetry",
            "fields[n].countMin / countMax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "SECONDARY_STRUCTURE",
          "why": "3 secondary register(s) at the recipe's own values. Pinned: 2:SPREAD — the pin takes the dimension away from the seed and makes it a project constant, which is the only creator-owned floor either runtime offers."
        },
